{#- One decision of the duplicate check's `decision` choice, described
    (`identity.build_items` renders it once per option). Vars: `decision` --
    "existing", "new" or "uncertain", the option's id, which `decide/user.j2`
    lists beside this text. Each description is that decision's bullet in
    the retired one-call prompt, word for word after its quoted
    word (`verify_templates.py`'s IDENTITY_OPTIONS holds each, by decision);
    the existing bullet's id sentence is `record.j2`'s. -#}
{%- if decision == "existing" -%}
only when a listed candidate is the same narrative question or obligation, so the row's beat simply moves that record forward.
{%- elif decision == "new" -%}
when the row is a different question, a continuation, or a related subplot: something that grew out of a listed record but is business of its own deserves a record of its own.
{%- elif decision == "uncertain" -%}
when the transcript cannot tell: the cited evidence and the beats do not settle whether the row and a candidate are the same business.
{%- endif -%}
